+/// SecondSonPC SSPC-002: a breakpoint exception at a runtime CPU patch that is being written (its
+/// first byte is an int3 meanwhile): waits for the patch, points the context back at the instruction
+/// and returns true; false for any other breakpoint. `misreported`: the same trap reported as a
+/// privileged instruction (the patch already replaced the int3 when the kernel looked at it).
+bool HandlePatchBreakpoint(void* context, void* exception_address, bool misreported);
+
+/// SecondSonPC SSPC-002: how many times HandlePatchBreakpoint sent a thread back to a patch (all
+/// of them / those reported as a privileged instruction).
+u64 PatchBreakpointsHandled();
+u64 PatchBreakpointsMisreported();
